        "Polynomial compatibility on the Boolean cube from disjoint-support separators \u2014 Alec Kriebel, v1.0.0 (2026-10-17). Problem30006210 / OWR-14299088-012, Austrin OWR9/2025 p445. Complete affirmative deduction for the exact TWO nonzero REAL degree-at-most-d multilinear polynomials on the UNIFORM sign cube: all full-Fourier-norm relative influences<=1/(4096d^8) ensure a common nonzero vertex. Disjoint supports require maximum influence>=1/(1024d^8). Constant coefficient included; common zeros allowed. Four-page note applies established Li2026 separator and OSSS2005 real covariance, with classical Markov/Bernoulli credit. No new separator/covariance theorem, novelty/firstness/global-openness certification, general distribution or other-group theorem claimed. Full ePrint2022/218 and2023/570 bodies inaccessible; exact scope gaps disclosed. Three mathematical families and three bounded priority approaches; four offline exact programs both modes and40 actual incorrect-result failures. Extensive AI assistance; unrefereed, no external human peer review/formal certification. Two successive fresh complete-package reviews passed identical release. https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1141 Published record: https://zenodo.org/records/23443301"
